{"id": "11th_tamil_u2_q149", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "hard", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_2", "lesson_id": "grammar_punarchi_vithigal", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "ko_il_kovil", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘கோ + இல் = கோயில் / கோவில்’ - இவ்விரு வடிவங்களும் வழக்கில் அமைந்ததன் இலக்கணக் காரணம் யாது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கோ (க்+ஓ) என்பது ஏனை உயிர் என்பதால் \"வ்\" வருவது விதி; ஆயினும் மரபு வழக்கில் \"கோயில்\" என \"ய்\" வருவதும் தொன்றுதொட்டு ஏற்கப்பட்டுள்ளது", "B": "அச்சுப் பிழையினால் ஏற்பட்டது", "C": "கோ என்பது உயிர் அல்லாததால்", "D": "இரண்டும் தவறான வடிவங்கள்"}, "explanation": "ஓகார ஈற்றிற்குப் பின் விதிப்படி 'வ்' வந்து 'கோவில்' என அமைவதே முறை; ஆயினும் தொன்றுதொட்டு வழக்கில் 'கோயில்' என்ற வடிவமும் இலக்கண அறிஞர்களால் ஏற்றுக்கொள்ளப்பட்டுள்ளது."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Why are both 'Koyil' (கோயில்) and 'Kovil' (கோவில்) grammatically sanctioned in Tamil usage for 'Ko + il'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Ending in vowel 'O', regular rule mandates V-glide (Kovil), while ancient literary convention equally sanctions Y-glide (Koyil)", "B": "Due to early printing typos", "C": "Because Ko is not a vowel", "D": "Both forms are strictly ungrammatical"}, "explanation": "By strict rule 'O' demands V-glide (Kovil), but deep literary usage historically ratifies Y-glide (Koyil) as well."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 36, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "11th Tamil, Unit 2, Page 36", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["Class 11", "Unit 2", "Grammar", "Usage Nuances"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T12:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T12:00:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
